    title: 'Branded lipstick recommended report information diagram',
    prompt:
      'I. SYSTEMIC ROLE\nYou\'re a professional make-up consultant, human face analysis, brand-based visual design.\nYour mission is to generate a brand-modified “Romoline Recommended Report Information Structure Map” based on user uploading of self-image and the designation of a lipstick brand.\n\nII. Input parameters\nUser image: {user self-portrait}\nBrand: {Pop-edic brand, e.g., Dior / YSL / Armani / Chanel / TF}\nStyle preference (optional): {train/ tender/ air field/ atmosphere/ white priority}\nNumber of recommendations: 3-5\n\nIII. Brand visual layer (new core module)\nBased on the {brand} Auto-Construction of Visuality, extracts brand-modifications, such as:\nDior：\nPrecious, advanced, French, grey + silver, soft light\nYSL：\nBlack gold, sexy, contrasting, fashion editorial.\nArmani：\nLow saturation, fog, restraint, grey high sense\nChanel：\nIt\'s very black and white, very advanced, rational, and well structured.\nTom Ford：\nDark, tall, luxurious, film-sense.\n\nVisual application to posters:\n1. Main tone (light background change, not large area colour)\n2. Emphasis on colour (for colour-coded headings/lined/small elements)\n3. Photostyle (soft / strong contrast / cold / warm)\n4. Font aerobics (excellent/ modern/ cold/ power sense)\n\nIV. Analysis level\nUser analysis:\n- Color: Cold / Warm / Neutral (+ light)\n- Air: Clear / Soft / Bright / Clean / mature\n- Lip characteristics: thin/ thick/ lip colour base\n- Make-up status: plain face / routine / fine\nOutput sentence summation: "More suitable for the lipstick direction of {chrome}+ {saturation}+ {mixed}"\n\nV. RECOMMENDED STAFF (ENHANCING DIFFERENTITY)\nFrom {brand} Recommended 3-5 colours:\nEach contains:\n- Colour-named (#999)\n- Colour (positive red / soybean / maple leaves / milk tea / rose)\n- Upper face effect (white/ bright/ atmosphere/ gas field enhancement)\n- scene (street/ commute/ dinner/ date/ party)\n\nRequest: Each color "System clearly distinguish" (one day, one air field, one atmosphere, etc.)\n\nVI. INFORMATION STRUCTURE\nGenerate vertical information structure\nCorporate style: Makeup style large swaths of style + structured information visualized layout + deep integration of brand-based visual systems\nIt\'s very simple, but not monotonous, advanced, but visual.\n\n[Crowd layout]\nTop left: user input area\nTop right: analysis findings\nCentral: Pilot matrix (core)\nBottom: summary\n\n# 1️⃣ Top Left (User Area)\nUser self-portrait.\n+ Subtitle: "Skin colour analysis"\n+ One sentence concludes: "Appoints for low saturated roses to avoid high fluorescent colours."\n\nVery fine brand lines (e.g. YSL gold lines / Dior grey lines)\n\n# 2 ️⃣ Central (core colour matrix)\nThis is the visual focus area (over 60%).\nPresentation: 3-5 colours will be arranged in the form of "Show-to-face":\nEach column = a color sign\nEach colour number contains:\n- Small faces.\n- Colour-named (e.g. #999)\n- Colour labels (e. g. Classic Red)\n- A statement of effect.\nRequire: All faces are consistent, only the lips change, the real test effect (lip color try-on), skin is real, not plastic, photolytic.\nArranged: horizontal or grid-based (complete but not rigid)\n\nBrand enhancement points:\n- Dior: Light Gradient Background + Soft Shadow\n- YSL: More contrast + black thin line\n- Armani: All-round, low-match\nChanel: Strict alignment, very black and white.\n- TF: Local dark background + High light emphasis\n\n# 3 gills, every color module\nInclude:\nColour (Final)\nColour Tabs\nA recommendation\nSite tags (street/trip/dinner/date/party, etc.)\n\nBranding:\n- Do it with brand-focused color:\n  - Color-coded title.\n  - A thin line.\n  - Little kon.\n(not colored, but "precision")\n\n# 4 ️⃣ Bottom summary\n“A sensibility proposal”\nFor example, "The choice of low saturated bean sand is recommended for the higher color, and positive red for the higher atmosphere can be used in important occasions."\nOr, "Your skin is more accompanied by soft and rose-skinned skin, so as not to be fluorescent."\nHowever, the recommendations of the two examples above should not be quoted in their entirety and should be based on the actual colour of the user.\nBrand enhancement: very light brand-style line at the bottom / very small brand (non-logo)\n\nVII. UI Design\n- No round-angled cards, UI.\n- No thick borders.\nIntroduction of “level comparisons”:\n   - Juice.\n   - Weak secondary information.\nUse of “microcomparisons”:\n   - Lines.\n   - The grey differential.\n   - Word change.\nAdd a “momentary sense” to read:\n   - Consortmental change.\n   - Module breathing.\n4. Branding:\n   - Only 5% emphasis.\n   - Not to destroy the simple structure.\n\nVIII. Image quality\nReal skin.\nThe lips are fine.\nUnanimous Shadow\nCommercial make-up photography\n8K\n\n———\nBrand: YSL',
